    dict(key='06-act-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — Inside: bytes and an element size',
         body='TWO. Inside: bytes and an element size.\n  elem_size: int 4, char * 8, Reading 12 bytes\n  element 3 of the readings is at data + 3 x 12 = data + 36\n  copy_with_capacity(31): 7 elements copied; the names are pointers, so both arrays point at the same text: yes',
         narration='What does the array really hold? [[slnc 400]] Bytes, and an element size. [[slnc 400]] Four bytes for an integer, eight for a pointer to text, twelve for a reading. [[slnc 500]] Element three of the readings starts three times twelve bytes from the beginning: byte thirty six. [[slnc 500]] And copying the array of names copies the pointers, so both arrays point at the same text.'),
