    dict(key='10-act-4', kind='console', title='Act Four — Insertion, deletion, overflow',
         body='FOUR. Insertion, deletion, overflow.\n  insert_at(2, Wed* 18 C): 5 shifts of 12 bytes each, n = 8\n  delete_at(0) removed Mon 21 C: 7 shifts\n  [Tue 23 C, Wed* 18 C, Wed 19 C, Thu 25 C, Fri 24 C, Sat 22 C, Sun 20 C]\n  n = 10, insert_at(0, Thu 30 C): overflow: the array is full',
         narration='Insertion and deletion work as before, with whole elements. [[slnc 400]] Inserting a reading at index two shifts five readings, twelve bytes each. [[slnc 400]] Deleting index zero copies the reading out, and shifts seven. [[slnc 500]] And when all ten places are used, the next insertion is an overflow.'),
